          "body": "\n- 2 November 2026 : a silhouette sees the outline only, a grey law sees slopes. Neither saw that my snout was twice too wide (x 0.5 at y 0.2, z 0.9, where the series has 0.2 to 0.25), that the ear was a plate along the head when it is a shell facing forward, or that the eye faces 24 degrees off the front. The measure that sees them : the same feature read in two or three views, its rays meeting at one 3D point. FR : une silhouette ne voit que le contour ; le même détail lu dans deux ou trois vues donne un point 3D, et voit la profondeur. (2 November 2026)\n- 2 November 2026 : tools, all in `scripts/Dracard/Comp/` : `PixelGrid.py <frames> <frame> out.png x0,y0,x1,y1 zoom step` a crop with a labelled pixel grid, so a feature reads to one pixel ; `Tri.py <cams.json> <frames> points.json` the 3D points and the gap in pixels per view (3 views under 3 px is trustworthy, above 5 the reading is not the same point) ; `LandmarkDist.py mesh.obj points_3d.json` the distance from the skin to each point, a depth error measured with no finished file ; `SurfaceCheck.py` casts a pixel on the mesh and compares its projection in the other views. (2 November 2026)\n- 2 November 2026 : `CompFit.py --landmarks points_3d.json --lm W` adds these points to the cost of the fit : the skin must pass through them. Use it from the blocks on, before the elements are placed, or every element sits on a wrong base. (2 November 2026)\n- 2 November 2026 : a frame near the border of the image gives a biased point (perspective, unknown exact FOV) : read a feature in the views where it is central ; the nose of frame 2300 is clipped and read 20 px off, frame 2440 replaced it. (2 November 2026)\n- 2 November 2026 : `HeadBuild.py` new settings : `mouth.depth` the slit stops at a fixed depth under the skin (VDB Reshape erode then union) instead of a slab across the whole head ; `eye.rot` and list radii, an oriented flat ellipsoid for ball and socket ; `teeth.pts` [x, y, z, scale] one tooth per measured place ; `flatten_n` a flatten across a slanted plane ; `ear.cut_skin` the hollow goes on into the skull ; `{\"p\": [x, y], \"snapz\": d}` a point kept on the front of the skin. (2 November 2026)\n- 2 November 2026 : a build that crashes keeps the old files : read the build report (the eye value, the protect list) before reading a board, I judged a stale board once after an indentation error hidden by `tail`. (2 November 2026)\n\n"
